intro='''<p class="kicker">2.0.0-alpha.11 · megaman2-audio-1 · development review</p><h1>Your ROM. Its native audio cues.</h1><p>Mega Man 2 US now fills Native Cue automatically: inspect 67 selectors, audition the native driver and turn a finite excerpt into editable tracker data. The earlier catalogs, Audio Discovery and original tutorials remain available.</p><div class="actions"><a class="button primary" href="NES_Forge.html">Open NES Forge</a><a class="button" href="Mega_Man_2_Audio.html">Mega Man 2 tutorial & formats</a><a class="button" href="Audio_Discovery_Guide.html">Unknown ROM discovery</a><a class="button" href="Native_Audio_Guide.html">Known-ROM audio guide</a><a class="button" href="Tutorial.html">Original game tutorial</a></div><div class="card"><h2>Try Mega Man 2</h2><ol><li>Open <strong>AUDIO → ROM Audio Library → Open NES ROM…</strong>.</li><li>Choose your own <strong>Mega Man 2 (USA).nes</strong>. The title becomes Mega Man 2 and Native Cue fills with <strong>67 selectors</strong>.</li><li>Select Music $00 or an Effect, then <strong>Inspect cue</strong> or <strong>Play native</strong>.</li><li>Use <strong>Preview editable score</strong> to review a finite adaptation, then import into the tracker.</li></ol><p>Music selectors include aliases and short jingles: 33 selectors, 24 distinct headers, plus 34 effects. Native audition and editable transcription have different fidelity; see the <a href="Mega_Man_2_Audio.html">complete tutorial</a>. Supply your own ROM; it is not included.</p></div><div class="card"><h2>Try an unknown driver</h2><ol><li>Open <strong>AUDIO → ROM Audio Library</strong>.</li><li>Use <strong>Open NES ROM</strong> to load <code>examples/Audio_Discovery/Discovery_NROM.nes</code>. This original example has no installed audio catalog.</li><li>In Audio Discovery, choose <strong>Record startup (resets game)</strong>, then inspect <strong>Writer evidence</strong> and <strong>Call / table / RAM leads</strong>.</li><li>Choose a writer and <strong>View selected writer source</strong>, or <strong>Export investigation</strong> to save the evidence.</li></ol><p>For another file, <strong>Open ROM for discovery…</strong> performs a static scan even if the emulator cannot load its mapper. Use <strong>Load this ROM in emulator</strong> before recording supported games. Recording advances the game and replaces its earlier Runtime Investigation trace.</p></div><div class="grid"><div class="card"><h3>Observed and inferred</h3><p>Static byte patterns stay distinct from executed, source-verified writers. Banked addresses, callers, queue/RAM references and indexed tables retain their uncertainty.</p></div><div class="card"><h3>Rank driver similarities</h3><p>Derived writer-context fingerprints from three recovered titles help rank code leads. A high overlap does not authorize a new native decoder or reconstruct a full audio library.</p></div><div class="card"><h3>Keep editing and building</h3><p>The earlier known-revision native catalogs, playback and finite tracker import remain available. Original guides, manual PDFs, game tutorial and examples are retained.</p></div></div><h2>Documentation and limits</h2><p><a href="Audio_Discovery_Guide.html">Complete discovery controls and limits</a> · <a href="Native_Audio_Guide.html">Native playback and editable conversion</a> · <a href="Guide.html">User guide</a> · <a href="Manual.html">Full manual</a> · <a href="Manual.pdf">Printable manual</a> · <a href="Tutorial.pdf">Printable tutorial</a></p><p>Discovery is a bounded investigation workflow. Complete unknown-driver song/SFX catalogs, original instruments/loops, generalized engine decisions and expansion-audio recovery still require validated decoders. Existing finite editable conversion omits DPCM and short-mode noise. Long excerpts can exceed a generated runtime’s normal capacity.</p><p>On Windows, extract the whole ZIP to a short path such as <code>C:/NF</code> before opening START_HERE.html. The archive has no redundant enclosing folder.</p>'''
intro+='<div class="card"><h3>Measured checkpoint</h3><p>'+str(gate['passed'])+' / '+str(gate['total'])+' automated cases across '+str(gate['suiteCount'])+' suites; '+str(browser['passed'])+' browser workflow checks. See <a href="VERIFICATION.json">verification records</a>.</p><p class="small">HTML SHA-256 <code>'+candidate['htmlSha256']+'</code></p></div>'
